{
  "requirement": "Outlining reads one file snapshot and parses its supplied bytes. Text search\nlists files in scope and searches their bytes. Structural search lists files\nin scope and parses their supplied snapshots. These operations share the\nfilesystem scope under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.provider_defaults.composition`.\n\n**Outlining reads one snapshot and parses its supplied bytes.**\n- In `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs`), `parse` on the `Memory` provider performs exactly one read (`reads == 1`).\n- The parsed source stays at \"version 0\" after a later `read` returns \"version 1\", so the outline comes from the same snapshot that was read.\n- The outline's `node_lines` contains that snapshot's text.\n- `list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search` parses the bytes a read-only `Primitives` provider supplies. It asserts the source text and that `fn[provided]` resolves in the outline.\n\n**Text search lists files in scope and searches their bytes.**\n- The same `Memory` test runs `search_text` under `SourceScope::under(\"src\")`.\n- The recorded event sequence ends with `list:src` and then a read of `src/one.txt`, which shows the default lists the scope and reads the files.\n- The assertions on match count, path, line and excerpt show it searched the bytes it read.\n\n**Structural search lists files in scope and parses their supplied snapshots.**\n- `structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope` uses a `CachedParse` provider that overrides `parse`.\n- It asserts the parse counter is 3 (one per search) and that the matches come from the overridden parse: path, selector `fn[cached]` and excerpt.\n- It asserts the requested scope `src` reaches the listing on all three searches.\n- It covers `limit` values of none, 1 and 0, with the matching completeness flags.\n- The `Primitives` test checks the same default with a read-only provider, and checks the error cases: a malformed rule, a mismatched resource, and an unknown language.\n\n**The operations share the filesystem scope from `requirements.sdk.sources.local_provider`.**\n- `gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs`) runs with and without a Git repository.\n- It checks that list, read, parse (outline) and text search all follow the same `.gitignore` rules, including nested files and exceptions, and exclude `.git` and `..`.\n- `built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope` shows structural search follows the same scope. Ignored files, ignored directories, `.git` and `..` are excluded, and a direct file scope works.\n\nI found no obligation that is missing a test or an assertion, and no marking gap.",
  "references": "052089c3443473951aef64cc577887d2fb947f5c6b07da6b25d20566dfc43caf",
